WEBVTT

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.400
Stand!

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.760
I told you to stand!

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.970
You're quite stubborn, aren't you?

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:22.660
Sebas!

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.170
You've stood up!

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.290
You finally stood up!

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.310
Sebas!

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.690
Well?

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.950
Which anime is it?

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.830
Do you remember now?

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:58.030
Get it together!

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:09.140
That was a terrifying nightmare.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.420
Mii-chan, is everything okay?

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:15.260
I heard a loud noise and a scream.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.430
I thought you fell off the bed.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:19.930
S-Sorry, I'm okay.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.180
You have bags under your eyes.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.190
Where did all those DVDs come from?

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:28.950
How should I explain...

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.110
I guess I could say it's homework.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.400
I'll lend you just a small selection 
of beginners' anime from my library.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.310
You're up early today, Mii-chan.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.630
Yeah, I have club work.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.960
You joined a club?

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.930
Really? What club?

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:52.710
Anime Club.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.800
World's First Space Elevator Constructed?

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.800
"Next stop, Space"

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.700
Anime Club?

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.210
Yeah.

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:58.550
I don't remember you liking 
anime that much, Mii-chan.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:01.000
It's okay.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.640
Minoa.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.650
I called your cell phone yesterday.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.070
My phone?

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.400
Is this what you're looking for?

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:22.010
Sorry, I was really busy 
and I couldn't answer.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:22.970
Sorry.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:24.700
That's all right, then.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:25.870
I was worried, is all.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.770
M-Morning, Kamiigusa-san.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:44.220
Good day.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.420
Morning.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.810
Good day.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.560
M-Morning, Kamiigusa-san.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.060
Morning.

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.660
<i>The</i> Kamiigusa-san?

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.220
Just said "Morning"?

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.820
Come!

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.820
<b>Anime Club</b>

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.820
If you like anime, join the anime club!!
 We shall serve tea and snacks and discuss anime!!
Time and place
Lunch time/After school
Club Building Room 3F

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.820
"Members wanted"?

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:02.290
Is that not why we came early?

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:03.760
Oh, right.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:04.330
I'll go put my bag—

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.530
Come on, come on!

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:08.890
What? What? What?

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.120
Get undressed!

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.090
H-H-Hey!

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.330
Wear this!

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:17.590
What? What? What?

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:21.590
Minoa?!

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.030
Wh-Wh-What is this?!

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:28.850
Bunny outfits are a standard 
for finding new members.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.470
Why?!

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.290
Let's get started.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.980
Anime Club, open to new members.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.810
Would you like to join?

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.990
P-Please take one.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.800
Say it louder.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.110
B-But...

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.490
Minoa, are you okay?

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:50.560
Don't you have to get to morning practice?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.900
Okay, Minoa.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.170
Yui-chan!

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.110
Good... luck.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.880
Yui-chan!

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.280
Well, let's continue.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.220
Anime Club, open to new members.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.080
<i>Screw it, I don't have a choice.</i>

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.230
O-Open to new members!

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:13.840
Open to new members.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:14.920
Please take one.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.190
Anime Club.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.480
Please take one.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.820
Anime Club, open to new members.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.110
Thank you.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:22.420
Take one, please.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.410
Please and thank you.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.410
Anime Club?

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.700
Why is she in a bunny outfit?

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.890
Please and thank you.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.200
Sign-ups start at lunch break.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.200
P-Please.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.040
Open to new members.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.400
Sign-ups start at lunch break.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.620
First, we'll need a supervising teacher.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.900
Someone who likes anime?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:31.170
No, I'd prefer someone who won't 
meddle with our activities.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:34.490
Is there anyone who'd be up for 
it this late into the semester?

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.490
I wonder if there's anyone bored enough.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:39.320
Man, I'm bored.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:41.960
Just crackin' my shoulder.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.220
Cracky, cracky, cracky...

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.510
<b>Dorayaki</b>

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.510
Anime Club, huh?

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:48.510
Please.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:49.890
Where's your room?

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.010
At the far end of the third 
floor in the club building.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.010
Far end of the third floor?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:57.090
I wouldn't mind putting my name down.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.620
Thank you.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:01.410
Don't count on me too much.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.520
I'm pretty busy.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:05.520
Sure.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:07.580
Want to go to the cafeteria?

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.620
I brought my own lunch today.

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:14.280
I hope we got some people that 
you can talk to about anime.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.730
By the way, did you watch <i>Thousand</i> yesterday?

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.390
It runs at midnight.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:19.540
I recorded it, though.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.870
How could you say that?!

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:24.290
As an Anime Club member, it's imperative 
that you watch shows in real-time!

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.170
R-Rear tire?

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.200
Real time!

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.050
I-Isn't it the same thing?

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:35.470
What if you hadn't watched it in real-time, 
and you accidentally saw spoilers online?

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.640
There's nothing more dishonorable
for an Anime Club member!

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.480
I-I'm sorry!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.480
<b>Anime Club</b>

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.390
Be sure not to miss <i>Gaka Stray Dogs</i> tomorrow.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:52.990
Wh-What's wrong?

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.170
Kouenji-san?

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.240
You're joining the club?

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:03.000
Yes.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:05.690
You like anime?

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.720
But you're always reading books 
with really complicated titles.

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:10.630
You don't seem like the type.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:15.900
Catchy, long titles are popular 
for light novels these days.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:16.890
Light novels?

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:20.310
Light novels are often 
fantasy and school dramas,

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:24.680
targeted mainly at middle and high school 
students, but they have a broad audience.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.280
The illustrations are cute, too.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:28.710
<i>The Melancholy of a Happy Vuvuzela</i>.

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:30.740
<i>Sold Out Offline</i>.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:32.420
They work well with anime.

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:34.220
They're even called "light novel shows."

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:35.810
Light novel boils?

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:37.840
What are you watching 
this season, Kouenji-san?

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:40.140
I'm keeping up with all 
of the light novel shows.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:41.540
You're watching <i>Ru:ZERO</i>, aren't you?

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.280
Yes, of course.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:44.540
Um...

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.730
Team Am or Team Emily?

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:49.560
I don't have a team. 
I think they're all cute.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.590
I think I like Pekelgaus's character.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.550
You are well-studied.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:55.910
You're tickling my brain.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:59.470
I think Am's voicing is perfect, too.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.310
They're having a perfectly 
clear conversation.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:04.340
You're always reading light novels,

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.720
so I thought you might 
be following anime, too.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:09.820
Do you read light novels, too, Kamiigusa-san?

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:14.450
I look up the originals sometimes, 
when the anime are really good.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.830
You don't ever read the light novels first?

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:17.790
I don't.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.100
Whenever a light novel I liked 
gets an anime adaptation,

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:24.200
I'm eager to see how my 
favorite scenes are portrayed.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.590
But doesn't it get boring 
when you see the anime,

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:28.710
if you already know how it plays out?

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:33.270
Then do you not enjoy your favorite 
anime when you watch it a second time?

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:35.520
Of course I do.

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:37.570
You notice things you didn't 
notice the first time.

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:40.470
And you know the story already, 
so you can pay attention to the art.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.390
You watch the same thing over again?

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:43.640
You don't?!

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.390
Sorry.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:49.650
So, well, I should read 
light novels, too, right?

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:54.150
I think you can watch the anime, 
if it has an anime adaptation.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:57.150
You don't understand a thing.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:58.240
Huh?!

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:00.070
Hold it.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:01.480
Calm down.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.080
'Sup?

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.230
Aoyama Erika of Class 3-B.

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:07.480
I'd like to join.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:09.080
You're a senpai from third-year?

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:10.640
Thank goodness.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:13.370
It's a bit intimidating when 
it's just us first-years.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.440
I saw you guys in your bunny 
outfits, recruiting members.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.290
You guys get it.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.590
Thank you.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.990
I never thought the fliers 
would work so well.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:23.580
Isn't this great?

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.100
Yes.

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:27.000
Thanks for coming, Kouenji-san.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:27.600
It's fine.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:31.370
So why don't we have Aoyama-senpai 
be the club president,

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:32.760
since she's a third-year?

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.070
That sounds good.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.070
Aoyama-senpai...

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.110
You can call me Erika.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.590
Erika-senpai!

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:38.860
Please be our president!

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.130
President?

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:42.210
Does that mean I'll have to be, all,

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:45.790
"Be awed at my beautiful technique" 
and "Let's not get caught off-guard"

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.620
and all that?

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:50.000
Wow, you really get it.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:50.550
What?

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:51.890
Caught off guard?

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:57.450
"I can see right through your plan" to leave 
the third-years with all the annoying work.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.130
That's amazing!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.510
See right through?

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.510
I wouldn't mind putting my name down.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.010
Thank you.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.500
That's four.

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:06.790
We just need two more.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.820
I have one person in mind.

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.520
He's just the guy.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:20.950
Danger comes.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:25.950
<b>Anime-Gataris, Assemble!</b>

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:33.090
Danger comes.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.310
Kaikai.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:38.650
The grimoire person.

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:39.970
Do you have a minute?

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:41.580
Don't talk to me!

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:44.470
There's mysterious energy matter 
escaping through this point.

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:46.570
He's putting up a barrier.

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:47.470
A barrier?

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:49.020
That's Kaikai.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.130
Class 2-B.

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:50.980
My name is

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:56.100
Musashisakai Kai!

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.250
Are you done with your barrier?

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.110
You're joining the Anime Club, right?

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:04.540
Anime Club?

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:09.440
I didn't expect you to 
get through my barrier.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:14.410
How would you even begin without me?

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:19.130
So on <i>Gaka Stray Dogs</i>, you're a fan 
of Dali, Picasso and Hiroshige,

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:21.680
and on <i>Old Game!!</i>, you like Run.

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:22.380
They're moe.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:25.050
So Arisucchi likes moe characters.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.890
Kaikai likes special power battle anime...

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:28.150
It's Musashisakai!

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:29.980
And Mikocchi likes light novels.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.890
I was a fan of <i>Gekisen Garumu</i>, 
so I'm looking forward to it.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.120
Minoacchi.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.150
Y-Yes?

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:36.530
You all right?

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:37.650
Can you keep up?

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.100
Honestly, I'm almost completely lost.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.030
You're all amazing.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:46.100
You must have a strong curiosity.

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:47.530
Why did you join the Anime Club?

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:50.360
It's fun, though.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.050
A lot.

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:52.120
Honestly...

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:55.680
It's like watching a whole 
new world open up before me.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:58.750
It seems you've opened the door.

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:01.390
So what's up with the cat?

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:03.050
Oh, that?

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:06.310
He seems to live here.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.760
A room with a cat, huh?

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:12.770
Well, let's meet up again after school, then.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.690
Yes, see you then.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:16.720
Yo.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:20.640
What is it?

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.280
You're quite unprepared, aren't you?

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.110
Unprepared?

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.060
It's only recently that you 
started liking anime, isn't it?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.700
Yeah, I guess.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.800
In that case...

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:34.610
Don't act like you know things.

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:35.990
Listen to them when they talk.

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:39.630
And don't <i>force</i> the conversation 
into something you like.

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:40.750
Okay.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.540
Thank you for the advice.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:43.340
Um...

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.130
What's your name?

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:45.930
My name, eh?

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.150
I've had many.

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.950
Can I call you Tama, then?

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:50.390
That's way too popular.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.630
Michael, then?

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:53.250
Tom?

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:53.860
Cheese?

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:54.580
Nyanko?

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:55.200
Baron?

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:56.300
Mikan?

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:57.390
Oh, Dora—

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:58.900
Stop right there!

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:01.230
Can I just call you Neko-senpai, then?

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.870
Fine, whatever.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.400
Okay, Neko-senpai.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.400
By the way,

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:08.910
did you take something out of that room?

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:17.540
I don't... think so.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.180
I see.

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.280
Close the door!

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:24.480
We'll make each other two promises.

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:27.050
Don't tell the others 
that you can talk to me.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.000
Always close the door after you open it.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:29.680
Okay.

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:40.180
<i>The choir competition committee 
will be meeting at four.</i>

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:43.790
Have you always liked 
light novels, Kouenji-san?

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:45.400
I've liked books since I was little.

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:46.950
And anime?

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:50.080
Ever since my favorite books 
started getting anime adaptations.

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.320
Oh, yeah?

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.160
That's amazing.

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:53.410
Amazing?

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.410
Yeah.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:55.770
Like, your dedication to light novels.

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.880
Your love for them.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.920
I don't mind being alone 
when I'm reading books.

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:05.520
I don't like being in the spotlight,

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:09.300
yet I have a habit of being abrasive when 
it's something I care about, like earlier.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.680
I'm a pain, aren't I?

00:15:13.190 --> 00:15:15.810
No, not at all.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:26.410
We'll have to check out the
meccas for our club trip.

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:27.380
Indeed.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:30.120
Tama, Tachikawa and Hachioji are a must-see.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:32.910
Kawagoe and Kawasaki will be mandatory, too.

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:34.580
Oarai, please.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:36.400
Aren't those all pretty close?

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.830
Why don't we go to Nagano for 
a skiing trip or something?

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:42.330
Sorry.

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:44.840
We'll have to go to the events.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.170
Next year's Anime Jipang.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.420
Anihaku and Anisute would be good, too.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.090
Comibut, please.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:53.970
Oh, what about cultural 
festivals at other schools?

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:58.150
Sorry.

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:00.100
<i>I'm totally not fitting in.</i>

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:04.730
Asagaya-san, we'll need 
you to study up on anime.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:08.400
I don't know where to begin, though.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:11.110
What is a "classic anime"?

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.490
What is a "classic anime"?

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:15.370
An interesting anime!

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:16.400
Correct.

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:18.490
But what is "interesting"?

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:21.370
Everyone has their own way 
of appreciating a show.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.440
Am I wrong?

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:24.120
That's true.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:28.130
There is one law governing what 
is considered a classic anime.

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:29.420
A law?

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:32.500
An anime where the character 
is running is a classic.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:33.320
Really?

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.130
What about the openings?

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.890
An anime with a badass 
older guy is a classic.

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:38.430
Older guy?

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:42.140
An anime where the supposed main 
character dies in episode three is a classic.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.850
Not in the final episode?

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:46.700
An anime with "God" 
in the title is a classic.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:48.770
<i>Does it receive some kind of blessing?</i>

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.380
An anime with a baseball 
episode is a classic.

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:54.040
What about tennis or basketball?

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:57.410
An anime where the protagonist's mech 
is a mass-produced model is a classic.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:59.910
I feel like you're talking to me in code.

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:02.490
An anime where the character 
barfs is a classic.

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:02.960
Barf?!

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:03.990
That's it!

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:03.990
Yup.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:03.990
Indeed.

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:07.670
This season's barf anime would be <i>Ru:ZERO</i>.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:10.460
Anime's way too deep.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:13.920
Did you understand last week's <i>Ru:ZERO</i>?

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:16.930
There's something that even you wouldn't get?

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.310
It's because you haven't read the original.

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:23.810
That episode skips right over a 
scene that was in the original.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.270
It would be long to depict,

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:30.420
and it's not directly related to the other 
scenes, so maybe that's why it got cut.

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:33.570
But with that scene, that episode 
would have made sense,

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.320
and it would have had deeper meaning.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:38.070
You would have understood 
if you'd read the original.

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:40.490
But it was cut in the anime.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:42.390
I didn't want them to.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.330
That's the problem with you.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:45.550
What?

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:47.510
Is there something wrong with talking 
about how great the original is?

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.100
Wait, guys...

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:51.770
I don't like it when you talk as 
though you're better than us

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:53.170
because you've read the original.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:54.340
I never said that.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:58.940
Whether you've read the original or not, 
I don't care, as long as you like the work.

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:03.850
But criticizing it because something that 
was better in the original got cut in the anime

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.810
is such a superficial way to look at it.

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:08.100
Say what?!

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:10.250
Calm down, you guys.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:14.140
Kamiigusa-san, we're finally 
here with people who like anime.

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:15.730
Let's enjoy it.

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:19.610
I don't think I can get along 
with this original story zealot.

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.120
You may leave if you'd like.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:24.940
Come on, we're one member 
away from having enough.

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:27.620
We don't need her just to have enough people.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:28.460
You're right.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:29.630
Kouenji-san!

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:32.630
I don't think there's anything 
for me to gain here.

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:35.130
Breaking up mid-flight on day one.

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:37.260
Not again.

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:39.450
Good day.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:41.260
That's wrong.

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:44.770
I think that's wrong, Arisu.

00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:46.520
Asagaya-san.

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:49.020
I think that's wrong, Miko.

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:54.940
I don't know much about anime.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:58.360
But I wanted to help you out

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.910
because there was something 
you can be so absorbed by.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.030
Being absorbed in something is beautiful.

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:07.380
Miko has her own preferences 
that she's absorbed by,

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:11.130
and she's trying really hard to express that.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:14.730
Arisu likes anime, and she wants 
people to talk about it with.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:17.560
Of course, that's a bit 
imposing and selfish, but...

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:21.050
I have an older sister that I 
get in a lot of fights with.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:25.250
Sometimes, I get sick of her, 
and I wonder why she's my sister.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:28.650
But my sister's obsessed with lacrosse,

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.810
and she's really awesome when she's playing.

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:32.770
And ever since I was little,

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:35.820
she would always cheer me on when 
I was absorbed by something.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:40.150
So I like people who work really hard.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.220
We finally got together 
with people who like anime.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:47.160
I'd feel bad for anime if we 
rejected each other over it.

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:52.820
What am I talking about?

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:54.330
I like your song.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:55.700
My heart's dancing.

00:19:56.680 --> 00:20:00.400
I hope you'll get to be able to 
talk about anime like you just did.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:01.680
It's you.

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:05.160
Huh? I, uh...

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:07.180
Thank you.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:10.890
How many members do you have right now?

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:11.830
Five.

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:12.970
Just one more.

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:15.310
That makes six with me.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:17.650
Uh, who is he?

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:19.200
Are you serious, Minoa?

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:21.200
He's Nakano-senpai from Class 2-A.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.570
He has a lot of fans in 
the upper classes, too.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:25.440
He's hot.

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:27.830
I don't remember him at all, though.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:28.860
Come on!

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:31.830
The sixth member isn't 
necessarily the least notable.

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:41.750
Looks like there are some who don't 
know of you at this academy, Aurora.

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:42.930
Kaikai.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.630
Musashisakai Kai!

00:20:45.630 --> 00:20:48.430
So, Nakano-senpai, do you like anime?

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.060
A <i>Dub Tone</i> T-shirt?

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:56.440
He's hardcore.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:57.980
That...

00:20:57.980 --> 00:20:59.580
That makes six of us.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:01.690
If you'll stay, that is.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:08.690
I'm only staying because 
Nakano-senpai joined.

00:21:08.690 --> 00:21:10.700
So sassy, Kouenji-san.

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:13.210
Shut up, Kamiigusa-san.

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:15.580
You can call me Arisu.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.650
Arisu-chan, Miko-chan...

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:19.730
You said our names without 
honorifics a minute ago.

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:21.460
I'm sorry.

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:24.720
I'll be in your care, my little kittens.

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:25.920
Kittens?

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:28.380
Yep, you're all my kittens.

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:30.470
Why kittens?

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:33.480
Because you're my little 
kittens, my little kitten.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:36.740
So anyway...

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:39.110
So Anime Club is online.

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:40.110
Yes!

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:43.400
Um... What?

00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:46.610
I hereby report that the Anime Club

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:49.280
is barred from using the club rooms 
indefinitely, effective immediately.

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:55.690
But we just started, though.

00:23:27.450 --> 00:23:30.180
An anime with a cat regular is a classic.

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:31.690
Obviously.

00:23:31.690 --> 00:23:35.140
Next time, the Anime Club 
is already met by a twist.

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:39.440
What's the twist, you ask? 
It's a turning point for this story, a—
